## Follow-up Questions
- How to handle watch failures or conflicts?
- How to scale the sidecar to many tenants?

This technical challenge evaluates expertise in multi-data center deployment, dynamic certificate lifecycle management, mutual TLS implementation, and tenant-aware routing patterns. Key assessment areas include: Vault integration for secure secrets management, Docker secrets and configs utilization, Nginx TLS configuration with mTLS enforcement, header-based tenant identification and routing, blue-green canary deployment strategies across data centers, automated bootstrap scripting, and comprehensive observability integration.

```nginx
server {
  listen 443 ssl;
  ssl_certificate /secrets/tenant.crt;
  ssl_certificate_key /secrets/tenant.key;
  ssl_client_certificate /secrets/ca.crt;
  ssl_verify_client on;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design per-tenant QoS with dynamic config in a multi-DC setup.

## Key Concepts
- Traefik RateLimit middleware, Redis store, per-tenant quotas, Docker Config
- TLS termination, hot-reload without restart, cross-DC coordination
- Request tagging with X-Tenant and validation of isolation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo middleware sketch: extract tenant and enforce quota from Redis
async function enforceTenantRate(req, res, next){
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant'];
  const quota = await redisGetQuota(tenant);
  if (quota.allow(req)) return next();
  res.status(429).send('Too Many Requests');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you audit cross-DC quota drift and recover from Redis replication lag?
- How would you test hot-reload behavior under config churn?
